course: dictionary
lesson: 6031
title: The sleep chemical
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Melatonin is a chemical your body makes by itself. It is made when it gets dark, and it helps you feel sleepy. «Bright screens at night make the brain release less melatonin, the body chemical that helps sleep.» The sentence tells you its job: it helps you sleep.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «...the sleepy hormone that rises when it gets dark.» Dark means more melatonin, so bright light can slow it down. A hormone is a chemical message the body makes, so melatonin is one of these messages.
explain: Melatonin can also be made in tablets or gummies, and a doctor may give it to help people sleep. The word is the same for the body's own chemical and the made one, so check the sentence to see which one it means.
fact: Melatonin is a natural chemical, called a hormone, that your body makes.
fact: Your body makes more melatonin when it gets dark, which helps you feel sleepy.
fact: Bright light, especially from screens at night, can stop the brain making melatonin.
fact: Melatonin is part of your body clock, the system that tells you when it is time to sleep.
fact: Melatonin is also made in tablets or gummies, and a doctor may give it to help people sleep.
exercise: When does your body make melatonin? | When it is very hot | *When it gets dark | When you are running fast | When you eat your lunch
exercise: «Bright screens in bed tell the brain "it's still day", so it makes less melatonin.» What does this suggest about melatonin? | It is a kind of screen | It makes you brighter | It is a type of food | *It is linked to darkness and sleep
exercise: Which word names the sleepy chemical that is also made in tablets and gummies? | *Melatonin | Sunlight | Jet lag | Screen
test: Why might a doctor give someone melatonin? | To make their hair grow | *To help them sleep | To mend a broken arm | To make them run faster
test: «Bright screens and exciting games keep the brain alert and can delay melatonin.» What does alert mean here? | Cold and wet | *Awake and paying attention | Very hungry | Fast asleep
exam: Which of these is true about melatonin? | It stops the brain working | It is a kind of bright light | *It is a natural chemical that helps you feel sleepy | It is only found in gummies
